'''LeBron Raymone James'''{{efn|Pronunciation of "LeBron": {{IPAc-en|l|ə|ˈ|b|r|ɒ|n}} {{respelling|lə|BRON}}<ref>{{Cite encyclopedia |title=James, Lebron |encyclopedia=[[Longman Dictionary of Contemporary English]] |url=https://www.ldoceonline.com/dictionary/lebron-james |access-date=June 24, 2026 |via=LDOCE Online}}</ref>}} (born December 30, 1984) is an American professional [[basketball]] player who plays as a [[Forward (basketball position)|forward]] for the [[Philadelphia 76ers]] of the [[National Basketball Association]] (NBA). Nicknamed "'''King James'''", he is the [[List of NBA career scoring leaders|NBA's all-time leading scorer]] and has won four [[List of NBA champions|NBA championships]] from 10 [[NBA Finals]] appearances, including eight consecutive appearances between 2011 and 2018. He has won three [[Basketball at the Summer Olympics|Olympic gold medals]] as a member of the [[United States men's national basketball team|U.S. national team]]. James is widely regarded as one of the greatest basketball players of all time.{{efn|Attributed to multiple references:<ref>{{Cite web |last=Smith |first=Mychal |date=January 10, 2019 |title=Michael Jordan, LeBron James, and the Best to Ever Do It |url=https://www.gq.com/story/the-goats |access-date=October 5, 2026 |website=GQ |language=en-US |quote=}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=October 15, 2020 |title=Michael Jordan vs. LeBron James: Everything you need to know about the NBA GOAT debate |url=https://www.espn.com/nba/story/_/id/30108804/michael-jordan-vs-lebron-james-everything-need-know-nba-goat-debate |access-date=October 5, 2026 |website=ESPN |language=en-us |quote=It's the never-ending debate among today's NBA fans: Michael Jordan vs. LeBron James.}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Lundberg |first=Robin |date=May 5, 2020 |title=Michael Jordan or LeBron James: Which GOAT Faced Better Competition? |url=https://www.si.com/nba/2020/05/05/did-jordan-or-lebron-play-better-competition |access-date=October 5, 2026 |website=Sports illustrated |language=en-US |quote=Michael Jordan vs LeBron James is the greatest argument in sports history. The GOAT if you will. And The Last Dance has just taken it to another level.}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=2022-05-04 |title=Look: Scottie Pippen Names His All-Time Starting Five |url=https://www.si.com/extra-mustard/2022/05/04/scottie-pippen-names-his-all-time-starting-five-nba-michael-jordan-lebron-james |access-date=2026-10-01 |website=Sports Illustrated |quote=The four-time NBA champion is often regarded as the best basketball player in history...}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Alcantara |first=Alexandra |date=October 3, 2024 |title=LeBron James' Son Says He Can Beat His Dad in 1-on-1 |url=https://www.si.com/nba/lakers/onsi/news/lebron-james-son-says-he-can-beat-his-dad-in-1-on-1 |access-date=September 30, 2026 |website=Sports Illustrated|quote=That's certainly confident, given that his father is often considered the greatest basketball player of all time.}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Bubel |first=Jennifer |date=2022-02-24 |title=5 things to know about LeBron James |url=https://en.as.com/en/2022/02/24/videos/1645720650_888883.html |access-date=2026-10-01 |website=AS USA |language=en-us |quote=LeBron James, who made his NBA debut in 2003 has been breaking records ever since and is considered by many the best basketball player of all time.}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Wicker |first=Kay |date=2025-10-20 |title=LeBron James loses major historic record to Kevin Durant |url=https://sports.yahoo.com/article/lebron-james-loses-major-historic-163944625.html |access-date=2026-10-01 |website=Yahoo Sports |language=en-US |quote=While he may be broadly considered the "GOAT," LeBron James no longer holds the record for the highest career earnings in the NBA.}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=2020-05-16 |title='He may have been the best ever': If LeBron James chose his 'first love' over the NBA |url=https://www.foxsports.com.au/basketball/nba/nba-news-nfl-news-lebron-james-high-school-football-career-stats-highlights/news-story/5f3c4759e889ecd46099c33ec6e9f5ba |access-date=2026-10-01 |website=Fox Sports |language=en |quote=LeBron James is considered by most to be the second best player in NBA history. According to some, he’s the greatest.}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Holleran |first=Andrew |date=2026-05-15 |title=LeBron James Snubbed From All-Time NBA Player Top 5 Lists |url=https://sports.yahoo.com/articles/lebron-james-snubbed-time-nba-030000397.html |access-date=2026-10-01 |website=Yahoo Sports |language=en-US |quote=LeBron James is widely considered to be either the No. 1 or No. 2 greatest NBA player in history.}}</ref>}}<!-- Editors: Before changing the preceding sentence, please see the lengthy discussion at [[Wikipedia talk:WikiProject National Basketball Association/Archive 49]]. It is the second thread from the top. -->

James ranks [[List of NBA career assists leaders|fourth in NBA career assists]] and [[List of NBA career steals leaders|sixth in NBA career steals]], and has won four [[NBA MVP]] awards, four [[Finals MVP]] awards, three [[NBA All-Star Game Kobe Bryant Most Valuable Player Award|All-Star Game MVP]] awards, the [[NBA Rookie of the Year|Rookie of the Year]] award, the inaugural [[NBA Cup]] MVP, and the [[FIBA Men's Olympics Most Valuable Player|Olympics MVP]]. He has been selected for the [[NBA All-Star|All-Star]] roster a record 22 times; to the [[All-NBA Team]] 21 times, including to the First Team a record 13 times; and to the [[NBA All-Defensive Team|All-Defensive Team]] six times.<!-- Please do not add "first team All-Rookie" as this is a minor achievement in the grand scheme of LeBron's accomplishments. It does not need to be in the lead.--> The [[List of oldest and youngest NBA players|oldest active player in the NBA]], he holds league records for the [[List of NBA seasons played leaders|most seasons played]] with 24, the [[List of NBA career games played leaders|most games played]], the [[List of NBA career minutes played leaders|most minutes played]], and the most field goals.

Born and raised in [[Akron, Ohio]], James gained national attention at [[St. Vincent–St. Mary High School]] and was heavily touted as a future NBA superstar for his scoring, passing, and playmaking abilities.<ref>{{cite news |last=Wahl |first=Grant |date=February 18, 2002 |title=Ohio High School Junior LeBron James Is So Good That He's Already Being Mentioned as the Heir to Air Jordan |url=https://vault.si.com/vault/2002/02/18/ahead-of-his-class-ohio-high-school-junior-lebron-james-is-so-good-that-hes-already-being-mentioned-as-the-heir-to-air-jordan |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230702103936/https://vault.si.com/vault/2002/02/18/ahead-of-his-class-ohio-high-school-junior-lebron-james-is-so-good-that-hes-already-being-mentioned-as-the-heir-to-air-jordan |archive-date=July 2, 2023 |access-date=July 1, 2023 |newspaper=Sports Illustrated Vault &#124; SI.com}}</ref> A [[prep-to-pro]], the [[Cleveland Cavaliers]] selected James with the [[List of first overall NBA draft picks|first overall pick]] of the [[2003 NBA draft]]. He won Rookie of the Year and quickly established himself as one of the league's premier players, leading Cleveland to its first NBA Finals appearance in [[2007 NBA Finals|2007]] and winning the [[List of National Basketball Association annual scoring leaders|scoring title]] in 2008. After winning back-to-back [[Most valuable player|MVPs]] in 2009 and 2010, he joined the [[Miami Heat]] as a [[Free agent (NBA)|free agent]] in 2010, a controversial move announced in the television special ''[[The Decision (TV program)|The Decision]]''.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|first=Tom|last=Withers|title=AP Was There: LeBron James dumps Cleveland for Miami|url=https://apnews.com/article/miami-heat-cleveland-cavaliers-nba-entertainment-sports-c842cbbffbd42a55ed8374fd1e1b4a93|work=AP News|date=April 6, 2022|access-date=April 15, 2022|archive-date=April 15, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220415214923/https://apnews.com/article/miami-heat-cleveland-cavaliers-nba-entertainment-sports-c842cbbffbd42a55ed8374fd1e1b4a93|url-status=live}}</ref>

With the Heat, James won his first two NBA championships in [[2012 NBA Finals|2012]] and [[2013 NBA Finals|2013]], earning MVP and Finals MVP honors both years. After four seasons in Miami, he returned to Cleveland in 2014, leading the Cavaliers to their first-ever championship in [[2016 NBA Finals|2016]] and ending the [[Cleveland sports curse]]. He signed with the [[Los Angeles Lakers]] in 2018, winning another title in [[2020 NBA Finals|2020]] and becoming the first player to be named Finals MVP with three different teams. After eight years with the Lakers, James signed with the [[Philadelphia 76ers]] in 2026.

James was the first player in NBA history to accumulate $1&nbsp;billion in earnings as an active player<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|first=Jasmyn|last=Wimbish|title=LeBron James becomes first player in NBA history to make $1&nbsp;billion in earnings while still playing|url=https://www.cbssports.com/nba/news/lebron-james-becomes-first-player-in-nba-history-to-make-1-billion-in-earnings-while-still-playing/|work=CBS Sports|date=July 22, 2021|access-date=July 24, 2021|archive-date=July 25, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210725082200/https://www.cbssports.com/nba/news/lebron-james-becomes-first-player-in-nba-history-to-make-1-billion-in-earnings-while-still-playing/|url-status=live}}</ref> and has been listed by ''[[Forbes]]'' as one of the [[Forbes list of the world's highest-paid athletes|world's ten highest-paid athletes]] fifteen times.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Magazine |first1=Forbes |title=LeBron James |url=https://www.forbes.com/profile/lebron-james/ |work=Forbes |access-date=7 July 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211110112038/https://www.forbes.com/profile/lebron-james/ |archive-date=November 10, 2021 |url-status=live}}</ref> ''[[Time (magazine)|Time]]'' named him as one of the [[Time 100|100 most influential people in the world]] four times—the most for a professional athlete.
